I0918 11:04:09.696496       1 strace.go:567] [   1:  21] agent-probe E write(0x7 /tmp/summary.txt, 0x1db0ad8f9800 "RFC 8446 specifies version 1.3 of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol, which provides authentication, confidentiality, and integrity for communications between two peers over a reliable transport. It obsoletes RFCs 5077, 5246, and 6961, and updates RFCs 5705 and 6066, superseding TLS 1.2. TLS 1.3 introduces major changes from TLS 1.2, including removal of legacy and static RSA/Diffie-Hellman cipher suites in favor of forward-secret key exchanges, mandatory AEAD encryption, encryption of handshake messages after the ServerHello, and a redesigned HKDF-based key derivation scheme. It also adds a 0-RTT mode for reduced-latency connection resumption, simplifies the handshake state machine, and consolidates session resumption and PSK mechanisms into a single new exchange. The document details the handshake and record protocols, cryptographic computations, extensions, compliance requirements, and security considerations necessary for implementing TLS 1.3.", 0x3ca)
